  "text": "She was engaged. Not married. In her village, saying yes to this could have got her killed. Gabriel gets sent to Nazareth. Not Jerusalem. Not the temple. A village nobody writes about. To a girl promised to a man named Joseph. Quick note, because everybody gets this wrong. Luke gives us the town, the fiancé, and his royal line. He never gives us her age. When you hear teenager, that is tradition talking, not the text. The angel opens with, \"Hail, thou that art highly favoured, the Lord is with thee.\" And she is troubled. Not by the angel. By the greeting. She is turning the words over trying to work out what kind of hello that is. Then the news lands. You will conceive. You will have a son. His kingdom will have no end. Now sit in the actual situation. She is engaged. Not married. In her century, in her village, this is not a blessing. It is a scandal that can cost her everything, and the law had opinions about women in her position. And her one question is not can God do this. It is: \"How shall this be, seeing I know not a man?\" She is not asking for proof. She is asking how. And when he answers, she says, \"Behold the handmaid of the Lord. Be it unto me according to thy word.\" Yes to a plan she could not verify. In a town that could count.",
